{
  "abstract": "We investigate sub-quadruple regular extensions of two-sided rational Diophantine quintuples in $(r, \\lambda, S_{ab})$, proving the sub-quadruple fifth elements are linear in $S_{ab}$ and their compatibility conditions cut out the Branch 1 elliptic sextuple surface $\\mathcal{E}_{\\text{Br1}}$ and twin-fifth surfaces $\\mathcal{E}_{F_1}, \\mathcal{E}_{F_3}$. We factor $R_4$ on regular fifths to define the 2D surface $\\mathcal{S}_{4, 2}$, collapsing on Branch 1 to a smooth genus-three curve $\\mathcal{H}$ of relation type $(5, 2)$ with unramified $d = 1$ descent and a new rational almost septuple $\\mathcal{S}_7^{(20/21)}$. In global coordinates $(r, \\mu, z)$, we construct explicit sextuple families and moving-parameter quintuples (with a global $2$-adic period-$6$ lock on $\\mathcal{E}_B$ eliminating $Q_4(k) \\equiv -2$), and factor $R_5 = \\frac{L_1 L_2 Q_4}{H K^4}$, establishing the Universal Triple-Square Section $L_1 = 0$, gauge involution $\\iota_K$, and rank-2 subgroup $\\Lambda(r) \\subset E(r^2)(\\mathbb{Q}(r))$. On the $3$-torsion inflection surface $\\mathcal{S}_{\\text{3-tors}}$ ($3 S_T = \\mathcal{O}$), we establish Tate normal form, the Orbit Cubic, and the Universal Master Syzygies in $(s, \\kappa)$ unifying Family IV, the classical Dujella–Kazalicki–Mikić–Szikszai family [7] (extended to an all-positive $22/28$ octuple $\\mathcal{U}_8^{\\text{DKMS}}(\\kappa)$ and section $Q_{\\text{ex}}$ on $\\mathcal{E}_Q$), and $\\mathcal{C}_{\\text{triad}}$ (with unconditional rank-$0$ $E_{15}$ closure of $1 + d_+ b'_{ac}(d_-) = \\square$ and 3-term linear spoke syzygies). On the four mixed-$R_4$ and double-product branches, we establish the $2$- vs. $4$-condition criterion, Mixed-$R_4$ Master Syzygies, shared $(s + 1) D(\\kappa, s)$ cancellation, an infinite family of $9/10$ quintuples on $\\mathcal{H}_{\\text{II}}$ ($\\operatorname{rank} E_{\\text{II}, C_2}(\\mathbb{Q}) \\ge 2$), general-$H$ syzygies with the $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{-2})$ norm $2$-descent closing $H = 1/3$, and the reciprocal Branch-B double-regulation surface $(u_d, u_w)$ with its Pythagorean Master Syzygy, a $5$-distinct nonzero $10/10$ rational quintuple at $(26/37, 24/37)$, and a Galois-stable $20/21$ almost septuple over $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{\\Delta_{ab}})$ at $(99/125, -284/625)$. No rational Diophantine septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Version 10 adding exact algebraic and arithmetic results on the reciprocal Branch-B double-regulation surface and moving-u elliptic curve E_B, plus all auditability refinements from the review of HWPk0AZSVEoEwZsZ (all verified in verify_paper.py and THEOREMS_AND_PROOFS.md in supplement.zip): (1) Reciprocal Branch-B Double-Regulation Surface (Theorem 7(6), exp38): Proved that once -P_8(u_d, u_w) = square, {c, d, f, e, g} is a 9/10 rational quintuple with (1+ax)(1+bx) = square for all 5 entries; exhibited the 5-distinct nonzero 10/10 rational Diophantine quintuple {3864/7163, -4845/2639, 319/1729, -382800/292201, -6344/3857} at (u_d, u_w) = (26/37, 24/37) where 1 + eg = (3071/1729)^2; proved that the 5 root-sum pairs collapse modulo Q^{*2} to two square-class pairs {\\Phi_{c,+}, \\Phi_{c,-}} and {\\chi_{d,+}, \\chi_{d,-}}, yielding a Galois-stable 20/21 almost septuple over Q(\\sqrt{\\Delta_{ab}}) at (99/125, -284/625); and proved the Pythagorean Master Syzygy (-P_8) + 4(u_d^2-1)^2 \\Phi_{c,-} = ((2u_d-u_w)(u_d^2+u_w^2-1))^2, globally obstructing u_w = 2u_d and parameterizing {-P_8 = square, \\Phi_{c,-} = square} in (\\lambda, \\mu); (2) Global 2-Adic Period-6 Lock on E_B (Theorem 5(3), exp38): Proved v_2(U(nP_0)) = 0 iff n = 6 (mod 12) where U(6P_0 + Q) = 3 (mod 8) on the formal group E_{B,2}(Q_2), globally eliminating the rank-2 twist Q_4(k) = -2 (mod Q^{*2}), and cited Paper 65v2 [16] for the complementary Chabauty closure of Y_B^2, G(k) = square; (3) Auditability Refinements from Review of v9: Included the explicit 2-isogeny homomorphism certificate for rank E_{II, C2}(Q) >= 2, explicit real-place positivity and 2-isogeny Selmer rank bound formulas in the H=1/3 norm descent, and precise bounded-search wording for the 5 boundary points on H_{II}.",
